}

docs {
  # Worker 1 health

  Identity, capacity and current load straight from the worker process.

  - `activeSession` — the session its SessionGate is committed to, null if free.
    A worker with a null activeSession is a spillover candidate.
  - `pendingSessions` — sessions queued behind the active one on this worker.
  - `inFlight` — broadcasts it is currently handling.
  - `queue` — should be `rsconnect.transport.voice.<workerId>`. If it reads
    `rsconnect.transport.voice`, WORKER_ID is not set and this worker is running
    in single-worker mode.

  Set `worker1-url` in the environment, e.g. http://localhost:5653/api
}
